# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Jekyll would skip a leading-underscore file, so
# `_headers` is listed under `include:` in _config.yml to get it copied into _site.
#
# RFC 8288 Link headers let a client discover the sitemap and the llms.txt summary
# without parsing HTML -- which is the point for anything that fetches with HEAD or
# doesn't run a parser at all.
#
# Verified against the live site: when several rules match one request Cloudflare
# *appends* the values, so `/` inherits the sitemap link from `/*` and must not
# repeat it. llms.txt describes the site as a whole, so rel="alternate" is declared
# on the root only, not on every page.

/*
  Link: </sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"; type="application/xml"

/
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="alternate"; type="text/plain"
